    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11269" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corpuscŭlum</span></b> , i, n.
		dim.
		corpus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a little body</i>, most freq. of atoms, <i><span class="en">Lucr. 2,
			152</span></i>; <i><span class="en">2, 530</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">4, 199</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cic. N.
				D. 1, 24, 66 sq.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">quantula hominum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Juv.
					10, 173</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Esp.: florum, i.e. <i>a collection</i>, Just. praef.
			—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> As a term
			of endearment: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">melliculum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Cas. 4, 4, 23</span></i>
			.</div>
